  "usage_note": "In American English **fall** is the everyday word for this season; **autumn** is also used, especially in writing. British English uses **autumn**. You can say *in autumn* or *in the autumn*, but no preposition goes before **last**, **next**, or **this**: *last autumn*. Names of seasons do not start with a capital letter.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "We met in last autumn.",
      "correct": "We met last autumn.",
      "note": "Do not use **in** before **last**, **next**, or **this** with a season."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "My favorite season is Autumn.",
      "correct": "My favorite season is autumn.",
      "note": "Names of seasons do not start with a capital letter in English, unlike the names of months."
    }
  ],
